From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backport-include: net.h: forward declare struct sockaddr_unsized

struct sockaddr_unsized was only introduced in Linux 6.19, but the
kernel_connect() compatibility shim for older kernels already uses the
new type in its prototype.

On an older kernel the type therefore gets implicitly declared inside the
parameter list, which creates a type distinct from the one ath12k casts to
in drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c, so the driver fails to build:

  qmi.c:4382:45: error: passing argument 2 of 'backport_kernel_connect'
  from incompatible pointer type [-Werror=incompatible-pointer-types]

Forward declare the struct inside the version guard so that both sides
refer to the same type and ath12k keeps building on 6.18.

---
--- a/backport-include/linux/net.h
+++ b/backport-include/linux/net.h
@@ -10,6 +10,10 @@
  * The in-kernel socket API takes struct sockaddr_unsized since 6.19.
  * Older kernels still expect struct sockaddr here.
  */
+/* Kernels older than 6.19 do not define struct sockaddr_unsized at all,
+ * forward declare it so drivers using the newer API still compile. */
+struct sockaddr_unsized;
+
 static inline int backport_kernel_connect(struct socket *sock,
 					  struct sockaddr_unsized *addr,
 					  int addrlen, int flags)
